tsrs patch to microsoft/TypeScript@39be28ba77f4 packages/typescript/src/api/async/client.ts
(applied by npm/sdk/sync-upstream.mjs; the selected original is recorded in npm/tsrs/UPSTREAM.json "patchedFiles").

Upstream, if the API server process dies or closes the connection while the async client is open, vscode-jsonrpc
marks the connection closed but never settles pending responses, so in-flight and queued requests hang forever
(with both tsgo and tsrs as the server). With this patch the client records the loss once (child "exit",
connection close or a failed write, whichever comes first; never after close()), rejects queued requests, disposes
the connection so in-flight requests reject, and rejects every later request, all with one Error whose message
starts with "API server connection lost: " followed by a best-effort detail. The source-109 close() timing dump
and idempotent close lifecycle remain upstream's; a lost connection records serverTimingError and still writes the dump.
The sync client is unchanged: its next call already throws at once, with the raw pipe error (EBADF/EPIPE)
or "Unexpected EOF while reading from child process (...)".
Also passes windowsHide: true when spawning the API server so console-less Windows processes do not open a visible console window.
